FROM gemma4:31b-it-bf16

# gemma4:31b-it-bf16 ships temperature 1 (with top_p 0.95 and top_k 64). Every score
# measured in this repo used temperature 0.1 sent explicitly by the bench, so the
# 77/80 on repohard was never demonstrated at the sampler a client actually gets.
# Pinning 0.1 here makes the measured configuration the default. The shipped
# temperature is measured separately as its own arm rather than assumed to be worse.
PARAMETER temperature 0.1
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 64
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1

# This model never ran away: 519 output tokens per repohard task, 94 per round, no
# truncation and no timeouts. The bound is insurance against Ollama's unbounded
# default rather than a fix for observed behaviour, and it is far above anything this
# model has ever needed. Matched to the 26B's value so the family behaves alike.
PARAMETER num_predict 24576

# Insurance only. Unlike the 26B, this model fabricated zero tool results across all
# eight repohard tasks, so these should never fire. Kept so both models in the family
# behave identically under a client that sends no options. See the 26B Modelfile for
# how <|tool_response> was obtained: it is the marker Ollama's compiled gemma4 renderer
# emits for a tool result, and therefore the one a native tool-calling client exposes.
PARAMETER stop "<|tool_response>"
PARAMETER stop "<arch_result>"
PARAMETER stop "<tool_result>"
PARAMETER stop "</tool_result>"
